  <item>
    <title>Oklahoma (SB 1488): data center moratorium — Rejected</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/oklahoma-sb-1488-ok</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-oklahoma-(sb-1488)-ok</guid>
    <pubDate>Sun, 23 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>SB 1488 (Sen. Sacchieri) would have barred new data centers of 100 MW or more until Nov 1, 2029 and ordered a Corporation Commission study. Introduced Feb 2, sent to committee Feb 3, never got a committee or floor vote, died at sine die adjournment on May 14, 2026</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Luther: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/luther-ok</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-luther-ok</guid>
    <pubDate>Sun, 23 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Town board ordinance pausing new rezoning applications and specific-use permit requests for data centers through Dec 31, 2026, and restricting approvals of applications already filed, while the town revises zoning for data centers and battery storage. Aimed at Beltline Energy&#x27;s proposed development, which the board discussed the same night without acting on it. The meeting drew a crowd large enough to be moved outdoors</description>
  </item>
